  "topic_en": "Continuation of Euler's tables of linear relations among the sums q^k and p^k (values of the multiple zeta-type series) for the orders m+n=6, 7 and 8, with the resulting expressions of q^k in terms of p's.",
  "transcription": "SERIES SINGVLARES. 175\nErgo\n$q^5 = p^2 - \\tfrac{1}{2}p^3;\\ q^4 = p^3 - \\tfrac{1}{2}p^6;\\ q^3 = \\tfrac{1}{2}p^3 + \\tfrac{1}{2}p^6;\\ q^2 = p^2 - p^3 + \\tfrac{4}{3}p^6$\n$q^5 = \\tfrac{7}{2}p^6 - p^2 - \\tfrac{1}{2}p^3$\n$q^5 = -\\tfrac{7}{2}p^6 + 3p^2 - \\tfrac{1}{2}p^3$ Ob $p^2 = \\tfrac{7}{4}p^6$ erit\n$q^5 = \\tfrac{7}{4}p^6 - \\tfrac{1}{2}p^3;\\ q^4 = -\\tfrac{1}{2}p^6 + p^3;\\ q^3 = \\tfrac{1}{2}p^6 + \\tfrac{1}{2}p^3;\\ q^2 = \\tfrac{37}{12}p^6 - p^3.$\nOrdo $m+n=7$\n$q + q^6 = p + p^7$\n$q^2 + q^5 = p^2 + p^7$\n$q^3 + q^4 = p^3 + p^7$\n$q^2 + q^3 + q^4 + q^5 + q^6 = 6p^7$\n$4q^3 + 3q^4 - 2q^5 = 6p^7$\n$4q^3 + 8q^4 - 2q^5 = 6p^7$\n$q^2 + q^3 + q^4 + q^5 + q^6 = 6p^7$\n$5q^2 + 3q^3 + 2q^4 + q^5 - 5q^6 = 10p^7$\n$10q^2 + 2q^3 + q^4 + 4q^5 - 10q^6 = 14p^7$\n$10q^2 - 2q^3 - 2q^4 + 6q^5 - 10q^6 = 8p^7$\n$5q^2 - q^3 - q^4 + 3q^5 - 5q^6 = 4p^7$\nvnde concluditur\n$q^6 = +4p^7 - p^2 - p^3$\n$q^5 = -10p^7 + 5p^2 + 2p^3$\n$q^4 = +18p^7 - 10p^2$\n$q^3 = -17p^7 + 10p^2 + p^3$\n$q^2 = +11p^7 - 4p^2 - 2p^3$\nOrdo $m+n=8$\n$q + q^7 = p + p^8$\n$q^2 + q^6 = p^2 + p^8$\n$q^3 + q^5 = p^3 + p^8$\n$2q^4 = p^4 + p^8$\n$3q^2 - q^3 + 3q^4 - q^5 + 3q^6 - q^7 = 8p^8$\n$12q^2 - 2q^3 - 9q^4 - 4q^5 + 7q^6 - 12q^7 = 18p^8$\n$30q^2 + 9q^4 - 6q^5 + 15q^6 - 30q^7 = 38p^8$\n$40q^2 + 4q^4 - 8q^5 + 20q^6 - 40q^7 = 42p^8$\n$q^2 + q^3 + q^4 + q^5 + q^6 + q^7 = 7p^8$\n$6q^2 + 4q^3 + 3q^4 + 2q^5 + q^6 - 6q^7 = 15p^8$\n$15q^2 + 5q^3 + 3q^4 + q^5 + 5q^6 - 15q^7 = 25p^8$\n$20q^2 \\ast + 2q^4 - 4q^5 + 10q^6 - 20q^7 = 21p^8$\n$5q^2 - 5q^3 + 6q^4 - 7q^5 + 10q^6 - 15q^7 = 13p^8$\n$q^2 - q^3 + q^4 - q^5 + q^6 - q^7 = \\tfrac{1}{2}p^8$\nhinc",
